{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Frontend Bundle & Performance Budget Watch",
  "description": "Monitors frontend dependency changes and bundle performance, detecting heavy imports, suggesting lighter alternatives, verifying code-splitting exists for large routes, and checking image optimization and caching headers",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "secure-gate-access/client/package.json",
      "secure-gate-access/client/src/**/*.js",
      "secure-gate-access/client/src/**/*.jsx",
      "secure-gate-access/client/src/**/*.ts",
      "secure-gate-access/client/src/**/*.tsx",
      "secure-gate-access/client/public/**/*"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "Analyze the frontend changes for bundle performance impact:\n\n1. **Dependency Analysis**: Check if package.json was modified - identify new dependencies and flag any large libraries (>100KB) added for small use cases. Suggest lighter alternatives where appropriate.\n\n2. **Import Analysis**: Scan modified JS/JSX/TS/TSX files for:\n   - Heavy library imports (lodash, moment, etc.) - suggest tree-shaking or lighter alternatives\n   - Missing code-splitting for large components or routes\n   - Inefficient import patterns (importing entire libraries vs specific functions)\n\n3. **Route & Component Analysis**: For modified route components:\n   - Verify lazy loading exists for components >50KB\n   - Check if React.lazy() and Suspense are properly implemented\n   - Identify missing dynamic imports for heavy features\n\n4. **Asset Optimization**: For modified public assets:\n   - Check image file sizes and suggest compression if >500KB\n   - Verify proper image formats (WebP for modern browsers)\n   - Ensure caching headers are configured for static assets\n\n5. **Bundle Analysis**: If tooling exists, run build analysis:\n   - Compare bundle sizes before/after changes\n   - Identify the largest chunks and suggest optimizations\n   - Check for duplicate dependencies across chunks\n\n6. **Performance Recommendations**: Provide specific actionable recommendations:\n   - Code-splitting opportunities\n   - Lazy loading implementations\n   - Alternative lightweight libraries\n   - Image optimization techniques\n   - Caching strategy improvements\n\nFocus on maintaining the performance budget and preventing bundle bloat while ensuring optimal user experience."
  }
}